// This source code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
//@version=5

// =============================================================================
// NQ / Mega-Cap Basket Z-Score Pairs Strategy (companion to the indicator of
// the same name in /indicators) -- FOR INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION IN THE
// STRATEGY TESTER, NOT AS A PROVEN PROFITABLE SYSTEM.
//
// PINE VERSION NOTE: written against //@version=5, for the same reason as
// the companion indicator -- no live TradingView editor was available here
// to compile/verify Pine v6-specific syntax, and this repo's existing
// script is also v5. Upgrade the version pragma yourself if you want v6.
//
// SOURCE / METHODOLOGY: replicates one specific rule from a completed
// backtest on SYNTHETIC daily data (2018-2026, train -> validate -> test
// split, 5 candidate pairs tested). NQ vs. an equal-weighted top-10
// Nasdaq-100 mega-cap basket had the best win rate (42.9%) and best
// Sharpe/profit factor of the five -- and STILL lost money net of costs
// out-of-sample: -6.4% return, -17.8% max drawdown in the test window. This
// script exists to let you re-run that same rule, segment by segment
// (Train / Validation / Test), against TradingView's own historical data as
// an independent check -- it is not evidence the strategy works, and a
// different result on real data than on the synthetic backtest should be
// expected and is the whole point of re-validating here.
//
// CHART CONTEXT: run this on NQ1! (CME Nasdaq-100 E-mini continuous
// futures), Daily timeframe -- every default parameter was tuned on daily
// bars and will not carry the same meaning on another symbol or timeframe.
//
// *** IMPORTANT LIMITATION: NQ LEG ONLY ***
// TradingView's Strategy Tester can only simulate orders against the
// chart's own symbol (NQ here) -- it cannot place a real, P&L-tracked order
// on the partner/basket leg in the same backtest run. So this strategy
// trades only the NQ side of the pair, directionally, using the same
// z-score signal as the indicator:
//   long spread state  (long partner, short beta*NQ) -> this strategy is SHORT NQ
//   short spread state (short partner, long beta*NQ)  -> this strategy is LONG NQ
// That means the "List of Trades" / "Performance Summary" you get here
// verify the SIGNAL (its timing, frequency, and the NQ leg's own P&L) --
// they do NOT reproduce the fully-hedged two-legged spread P&L or costs
// that the original synthetic backtest measured. Full two-legged
// verification requires an external multi-asset backtesting environment,
// same as the original backtest used.
//
// NO-REPAINT DESIGN: identical to the companion indicator -- beta/spread/
// zscore recompute every bar, but every entry/exit/stop DECISION is
// evaluated off zscore[1] (the previous, fully confirmed bar's close), so a
// decision made "on" bar T only ever uses data knowable at T's open. Orders
// are configured to fill at that same bar's close (process_orders_on_close
// = true below) -- i.e. "decide from yesterday's confirmed close, transact
// by today's close" -- a single, consistent, conservative day of lag from
// information to execution, and it keeps this strategy's fills bar-aligned
// with the indicator's plotted markers for direct comparison.
//
// COSTS: commission/slippage defaults are set below in the strategy()
// declaration (Pine requires literal, not input-driven, values there).
// Override them without touching code via the Strategy Tester's own
// "Properties" tab (commission, slippage, initial capital, order size).
//
// ON-CHART ENTRY / TAKE-PROFIT / STOP-LOSS: shown both in the z-score pane
// (native units) and, via force_overlay, directly on the NQ candles in
// price terms (see the NQ PRICE PROJECTION block). The NQ price entry is
// the actual fill price; NQ price TP/SL are a LIVE estimate re-solved every
// bar from today's beta/spread stats, so they will visibly drift over a
// trade's life -- display only, the real orders are still driven by the
// confirmed z-score crossing the exit/stop band, never by price itself.
//
// PROP FIRM RISK MANAGEMENT: position size (qty, in NQ or MNQ contracts)
// is computed per trade from the live implied stop distance, capped so a
// single entry risks no more than Risk Per Trade % of Max Account Loss --
// default_qty_value below is just a fallback; every strategy.entry() call
// overrides it with this computed qty. strategy.risk.max_drawdown() is
// also armed as a native backstop: once equity draws down by Max Account
// Loss from its peak, Pine force-flattens and blocks further orders for
// the rest of the run. This backtests the RULE, not a live guarantee --
// it cannot talk to your prop firm's platform, and gap risk can still
// realize a larger loss than a single trade was sized for.
//
// INTRADAY ACCOMMODATION: two things specifically corrupt this signal on
// timeframes finer than Daily, and both have an opt-out toggle below (see
// the companion indicator's identical note for the full rationale). (1) An
// RTH Session Filter suppresses signal evaluation entirely outside NYSE
// regular hours, since the basket stocks are stale/forward-filled while NQ
// keeps moving outside that window -- a pure session-mismatch artifact.
// (2) Auto-Scale Windows for Intraday stretches hedgeWindow/lookbackZ by
// the chart's estimated bars-per-RTH-day, so "90" still spans roughly 90
// TRADING DAYS of memory rather than collapsing to a few hours of raw
// intraday bars. Both default on. They fix the specific failure mode that
// produced ~220 trades / ~18% win rate on a 5-minute chart during testing
// -- they do NOT mean intraday threshold behavior has been independently
// validated, only that the two most obvious artifact sources are addressed.
// =============================================================================
strategy("NQ / Basket Z-Score Pairs Strategy [NQ leg]", shorttitle = "NQ/Basket Z Strat", overlay = false, initial_capital = 100000, currency = currency.USD, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 2.0, slippage = 2, process_orders_on_close = true, calc_on_every_tick = false)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUTS -- identical strategy inputs to the companion indicator, plus the
// Train / Validation / Test segment controls.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
grpPartner = "Partner Instrument"
grpBasket  = "Basket Constituents (used only when Partner = Equal-Weight Basket)"
grpStrat   = "Strategy Parameters (tuned on NQ1! Daily -- see header)"
grpSession = "Intraday Accommodation (only matters off the Daily chart)"
grpRisk    = "Prop Firm Risk Management"
grpSeg     = "Backtest Segment (Train -> Validate -> Test)"
grpDisplay = "Display"

partnerChoice = input.string("Equal-Weight Basket", "Partner Instrument", options = ["Equal-Weight Basket", "QQQ", "ES1!", "XLK"], group = grpPartner)

sym1  = input.symbol("AAPL",  "Constituent 1",  group = grpBasket)
sym2  = input.symbol("MSFT",  "Constituent 2",  group = grpBasket)
sym3  = input.symbol("NVDA",  "Constituent 3",  group = grpBasket)
sym4  = input.symbol("AMZN",  "Constituent 4",  group = grpBasket)
sym5  = input.symbol("META",  "Constituent 5",  group = grpBasket)
sym6  = input.symbol("GOOGL", "Constituent 6",  group = grpBasket)
sym7  = input.symbol("AVGO",  "Constituent 7",  group = grpBasket)
sym8  = input.symbol("TSLA",  "Constituent 8",  group = grpBasket)
sym9  = input.symbol("COST",  "Constituent 9",  group = grpBasket)
sym10 = input.symbol("NFLX",  "Constituent 10", group = grpBasket)

hedgeWindow = input.int(90, "Hedge Ratio Window (bars)", minval = 5, group = grpStrat)
lookbackZ   = input.int(90, "Z-Score Lookback (bars)", minval = 5, group = grpStrat)
entryZ      = input.float(2.0, "Entry Threshold |z|", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpStrat)
exitZ       = input.float(0.5, "Exit-to-Flat Threshold |z|", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = grpStrat)
stopZ       = input.float(3.5, "Hard Stop Threshold |z|", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpStrat)

// See INTRADAY ACCOMMODATION in the header for why these exist. Both
// default on, since off the Daily chart they fix the specific artifact
// that produced ~220 trades / ~18% win rate during testing.
useSessionFilter = input.bool(true, "Restrict Signals to Regular Trading Hours (NYSE)", group = grpSession, tooltip = "Ignored on the Daily chart. On intraday timeframes, only evaluates entries/exits/stops while the basket stocks are actively trading (09:30-16:00 by default) -- outside that window their price is stale/forward-filled while NQ keeps moving, which is what corrupts the spread.")
sessionWindow     = input.session("0930-1600", "RTH Session", group = grpSession)
sessionTZ         = input.string("America/New_York", "Session Timezone", group = grpSession)
autoScaleWindows  = input.bool(true, "Auto-Scale Hedge/Z-Score Windows for Intraday", group = grpSession, tooltip = "Ignored on the Daily chart. Stretches Hedge Ratio Window and Z-Score Lookback by the chart's estimated bars-per-RTH-day, so '90' still spans roughly 90 TRADING DAYS of memory instead of collapsing to a few hours of 5-minute bars.")

// See the companion indicator's identical block for the full rationale.
maxLossUSD      = input.float(2000, "Max Account Loss ($)", minval = 1, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Hard ceiling on drawdown from the equity peak (e.g. a prop firm's max loss / trailing drawdown rule). Armed below via strategy.risk.max_drawdown() as a native backstop.")
riskPerTradePct = input.float(10, "Risk Per Trade (% of Max Loss)", minval = 1, maxval = 100, step = 1, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Caps a single trade's stop-loss risk at this fraction of Max Account Loss -- deliberately conservative, since this pair lost money net of costs even in its best backtest segment.")

// IMPORTANT: unlike the companion indicator (which only displays its own
// estimate and has no "Contract Type" dropdown to get out of sync), this
// strategy's qty is settled by Pine using the CHART'S OWN symbol point
// value -- a dropdown here would silently mis-size every trade if it
// didn't match what the chart is actually running on. syminfo.pointvalue
// is the $ per 1.0 index point for whatever symbol this script is loaded
// on, so it always matches what Pine will actually realize. To size in
// MNQ (micro, $2/pt) terms instead of full NQ ($20/pt), load this script
// on the MNQ1! chart rather than NQ1! -- position sizing below adapts
// automatically either way.
pointValue = syminfo.pointvalue

// Native Pine risk rule: once equity drops maxLossUSD from its peak, Pine
// force-closes the open position and rejects further orders for the rest
// of the run -- the backtest-level backstop behind the position sizing
// below (see PROP FIRM RISK MANAGEMENT in the header).
strategy.risk.max_drawdown(maxLossUSD, strategy.cash)

// Which of the three windows below is actually traded. Flip this and re-run
// to compare segments, matching the original backtest's methodology.
segmentChoice = input.string("Test (2024-01-01 to 2026-08-23)", "Active Segment", options = ["Train (2018-01-01 to 2021-12-31)", "Validation (2022-01-01 to 2023-12-31)", "Test (2024-01-01 to 2026-08-23)", "All History (ignore segment dates)"], group = grpSeg)

trainStart = input.time(timestamp(2018, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),    "Train Start",      group = grpSeg)
trainEnd   = input.time(timestamp(2021, 12, 31, 23, 59, 59), "Train End",      group = grpSeg)
valStart   = input.time(timestamp(2022, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),    "Validation Start", group = grpSeg)
valEnd     = input.time(timestamp(2023, 12, 31, 23, 59, 59), "Validation End", group = grpSeg)
testStart  = input.time(timestamp(2024, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),    "Test Start",       group = grpSeg)
testEnd    = input.time(timestamp(2026, 8, 23, 23, 59, 59), "Test End",        group = grpSeg)

showTable   = input.bool(true, "Show Stats Table", group = grpDisplay)
showMarkers = input.bool(true, "Show Entry/Exit/Stop Markers", group = grpDisplay)
showBg      = input.bool(true, "Show Position Background Shading", group = grpDisplay)
showLevels  = input.bool(true, "Show Price Reference Bands on NQ Chart (always on, not just while in a trade)", group = grpDisplay)

segStart = segmentChoice == "Train (2018-01-01 to 2021-12-31)"      ? trainStart :
     segmentChoice == "Validation (2022-01-01 to 2023-12-31)" ? valStart   :
     segmentChoice == "Test (2024-01-01 to 2026-08-23)"       ? testStart  : timestamp(1970, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0)

segEnd = segmentChoice == "Train (2018-01-01 to 2021-12-31)"      ? trainEnd :
     segmentChoice == "Validation (2022-01-01 to 2023-12-31)" ? valEnd   :
     segmentChoice == "Test (2024-01-01 to 2026-08-23)"       ? testEnd  : timestamp(2099, 12, 31, 23, 59, 59)

inSegment = time >= segStart and time <= segEnd

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TIMEFRAME CHECK + INTRADAY ACCOMMODATION -- every default parameter was
// tuned on DAILY bars. See the companion indicator's identical block for
// the full rationale (stock legs vs. NQ's near-24/5 session mismatch).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
inRTH     = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessionWindow, sessionTZ))
sessionOK = timeframe.isdaily or timeframe.isweekly or timeframe.ismonthly or not useSessionFilter or inRTH

minutesPerBar  = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) / 60
barsPerRTHDay  = minutesPerBar > 0 ? math.max(1, math.round(390 / minutesPerBar)) : 1
scaleWindows   = autoScaleWindows and not timeframe.isdaily and not timeframe.isweekly and not timeframe.ismonthly
effHedgeWindow = scaleWindows ? hedgeWindow * barsPerRTHDay : hedgeWindow
effLookbackZ   = scaleWindows ? lookbackZ   * barsPerRTHDay : lookbackZ

intradayAdapted = not timeframe.isdaily and useSessionFilter and autoScaleWindows
showTfAlarm      = not timeframe.isdaily and not intradayAdapted

var label tfWarnLbl = na
if barstate.islast
    label.delete(tfWarnLbl)
    if showTfAlarm
        tfWarnLbl := label.new(bar_index, na, text = "⚠ WRONG TIMEFRAME\nTuned for the DAILY chart -- current: " + timeframe.period + "\nEnable RTH Session Filter + Auto-Scale Windows\n(Intraday Accommodation group) or switch to Daily.", style = label.style_label_down, yloc = yloc.abovebar, color = color.new(color.orange, 0), textcolor = color.black, size = size.large, force_overlay = true)
    else if intradayAdapted
        tfWarnLbl := label.new(bar_index, na, text = "ℹ INTRADAY MODE (" + timeframe.period + "): RTH-filtered, windows auto-scaled to ~" + str.tostring(effHedgeWindow) + " bars.\nStill not independently validated intraday -- see header.", style = label.style_label_down, yloc = yloc.abovebar, color = color.new(color.blue, 0), textcolor = color.white, size = size.normal, force_overlay = true)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// BASKET CONSTRUCTION -- identical to the companion indicator (see its
// comments for the "first bar in view" / persistent-var-per-call-site note).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
c1  = request.security(sym1,  timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
c2  = request.security(sym2,  timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
c3  = request.security(sym3,  timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
c4  = request.security(sym4,  timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
c5  = request.security(sym5,  timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
c6  = request.security(sym6,  timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
c7  = request.security(sym7,  timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
c8  = request.security(sym8,  timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
c9  = request.security(sym9,  timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
c10 = request.security(sym10, timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

f_normalize(src) =>
    var float base = na
    if na(base) and not na(src)
        base := src
    na(base) ? na : src / base

n1  = f_normalize(c1)
n2  = f_normalize(c2)
n3  = f_normalize(c3)
n4  = f_normalize(c4)
n5  = f_normalize(c5)
n6  = f_normalize(c6)
n7  = f_normalize(c7)
n8  = f_normalize(c8)
n9  = f_normalize(c9)
n10 = f_normalize(c10)

basketRaw = (n1 + n2 + n3 + n4 + n5 + n6 + n7 + n8 + n9 + n10) / 10
basket    = basketRaw * 1000

singleTicker = partnerChoice == "QQQ" ? "QQQ" : partnerChoice == "ES1!" ? "ES1!" : partnerChoice == "XLK" ? "XLK" : "QQQ"
singleClose  = request.security(singleTicker, timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

partner = partnerChoice == "Equal-Weight Basket" ? basket : singleClose

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// BETA / SPREAD / Z-SCORE -- identical derivation to the companion indicator.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
logNQ      = math.log(close)
logPartner = math.log(partner)

// Uses effHedgeWindow/effLookbackZ (see TIMEFRAME CHECK + INTRADAY
// ACCOMMODATION above) -- identical to hedgeWindow/lookbackZ on the Daily
// chart; stretched on intraday charts when Auto-Scale is enabled.
beta   = ta.correlation(logPartner, logNQ, effHedgeWindow) * ta.stdev(logPartner, effHedgeWindow) / ta.stdev(logNQ, effHedgeWindow)
spread = logPartner - beta * logNQ

// spreadMean/spreadStdev named separately so the NQ PRICE PROJECTION block
// below can reuse the exact same rolling stats the z-score was built from.
spreadMean  = ta.sma(spread, effLookbackZ)
spreadStdev = ta.stdev(spread, effLookbackZ)
zscore      = (spread - spreadMean) / spreadStdev

// One-bar lag for every trading decision -- see header NO-REPAINT DESIGN note.
zSig = zscore[1]

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// NQ PRICE PROJECTION -- inverts the z-score formula to express a target
// z-value as an implied NQ price (see the companion indicator's identical
// block for the full derivation/rationale). LIVE estimate, not a fixed
// target: recomputed every bar from today's beta/spreadMean/spreadStdev.
// GUARD: a small beta or oversized spreadStdev (e.g. on a timeframe this
// wasn't tuned for) can blow the exponent up so math.exp() overflows toward
// infinity. Treat any result more than 5x away from the current NQ price as
// unreliable and return na rather than displaying a meaningless number.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
f_impliedNQPrice(zTarget) =>
    raw = math.exp((logPartner - spreadMean - zTarget * spreadStdev) / beta)
    raw > close / 5 and raw < close * 5 ? raw : na

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STATE MACHINE -- mirrors the companion indicator's position states, but
// drives real strategy.entry()/strategy.close_all() orders on the NQ leg.
// Named posState, not "position", because Pine reserves the identifier
// `position` as a built-in namespace (position.top_right etc., used below
// by table.new()) -- reusing it as a variable would shadow that namespace.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
var int posState = 0   // 0 = flat, 1 = long spread (=> short NQ), -1 = short spread (=> long NQ)

// Entry / take-profit / stop-loss levels for the open trade, in z-score
// units -- see the companion indicator's identical comment for why not an
// NQ dollar price (beta and the spread's rolling mean/stdev shift every
// bar, so a fixed price target/stop isn't well-defined here). These are
// display-only: the actual orders below are still driven by stopSig/exitSig
// (the confirmed z-score crossing the stop/exit band), not by price
// crossing these levels.
var float entryLevel = na
var float tpLevel     = na
var float slLevel     = na
var label entryLbl    = na
var label tpLbl        = na
var label slLbl        = na

// Same three levels, on the NQ price axis, so they draw directly on the NQ
// candles too. entryPriceNQ is a fixed, historical fill price; tpPriceNQ/
// slPriceNQ are the LIVE implied-price estimate (see NQ PRICE PROJECTION
// above), computed fresh every bar below rather than stored as `var`.
var float entryPriceNQ  = na
var label entryPriceLbl = na

// Position-sizing / loss-governor state -- see the companion indicator's
// identical comment. cumPnlUSD/killSwitch here are INFORMATIONAL (for the
// table and a matching on-chart warning); the real enforcement is
// strategy.risk.max_drawdown(), already armed above.
var float slPriceAtEntry = na
var int   tradeContracts = 0
var float cumPnlUSD      = 0.0
var bool  killSwitch     = false

// sessionOK (see TIMEFRAME CHECK + INTRADAY ACCOMMODATION above) gates
// EVERY decision -- entries, exits, and stops -- so a position already
// open when the stock market closes simply holds, untouched by the
// artificial spread swings that stale forward-filled stock data would
// otherwise create, until RTH resumes.
haveSignal = not na(zSig) and sessionOK

// Prospective stop distance / position size for EACH possible direction,
// evaluated every bar with live data -- BEFORE any entry decision -- so a
// trade whose stop is too wide to size even 1 contract within the
// per-trade risk budget is skipped entirely rather than forced through.
riskBudgetUSD = maxLossUSD * riskPerTradePct / 100

prospSlLong  = f_impliedNQPrice(-stopZ)
prospSlShort = f_impliedNQPrice(stopZ)
prospDistLong  = na(prospSlLong)  ? na : math.abs(close - prospSlLong)
prospDistShort = na(prospSlShort) ? na : math.abs(close - prospSlShort)
prospContractsLong  = (not na(prospDistLong)  and prospDistLong  > 0) ? math.floor(riskBudgetUSD / (prospDistLong  * pointValue)) : 0
prospContractsShort = (not na(prospDistShort) and prospDistShort > 0) ? math.floor(riskBudgetUSD / (prospDistShort * pointValue)) : 0

longEntrySig  = haveSignal and inSegment and not killSwitch and posState == 0 and zSig < -entryZ and prospContractsLong  >= 1
shortEntrySig = haveSignal and inSegment and not killSwitch and posState == 0 and zSig >  entryZ and prospContractsShort >= 1
stopSig       = haveSignal and posState != 0 and math.abs(zSig) > stopZ
exitSig       = haveSignal and posState != 0 and not stopSig and math.abs(zSig) < exitZ
segmentExitSig = not inSegment and posState != 0

// Snapshot BEFORE any close-handling block below resets posState to 0, so
// the P&L calc after them still knows which direction is being closed.
closingPosState = posState

if longEntrySig
    // Long spread = long partner, short beta*NQ -> the tradeable NQ leg is short.
    strategy.entry("ShortNQ", strategy.short, qty = prospContractsLong, comment = "LongSpread")
    posState       := 1
    entryLevel     := zSig
    tpLevel        := -exitZ
    slLevel        := -stopZ
    entryPriceNQ   := close
    slPriceAtEntry := prospSlLong
    tradeContracts := prospContractsLong
    entryLbl := label.new(bar_index, zSig,   text = "ENTRY " + str.tostring(zSig, "#.##"), style = label.style_triangleup,  yloc = yloc.price, color = color.new(color.green, 0), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
    tpLbl    := label.new(bar_index, tpLevel, text = "TP " + str.tostring(tpLevel, "#.##"), style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.teal, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
    slLbl    := label.new(bar_index, slLevel, text = "SL " + str.tostring(slLevel, "#.##"), style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.red, 20),  textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
    entryPriceLbl := label.new(bar_index, na, text = "SHORT NQ ENTRY\n" + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + "\n" + str.tostring(tradeContracts) + " contract(s)", style = label.style_triangledown, yloc = yloc.abovebar, color = color.new(color.red, 0), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, force_overlay = true)

if shortEntrySig
    // Short spread = short partner, long beta*NQ -> the tradeable NQ leg is long.
    strategy.entry("LongNQ", strategy.long, qty = prospContractsShort, comment = "ShortSpread")
    posState       := -1
    entryLevel     := zSig
    tpLevel        := exitZ
    slLevel        := stopZ
    entryPriceNQ   := close
    slPriceAtEntry := prospSlShort
    tradeContracts := prospContractsShort
    entryLbl := label.new(bar_index, zSig,   text = "ENTRY " + str.tostring(zSig, "#.##"), style = label.style_triangledown, yloc = yloc.price, color = color.new(color.red, 0),  textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
    tpLbl    := label.new(bar_index, tpLevel, text = "TP " + str.tostring(tpLevel, "#.##"), style = label.style_label_left,  color = color.new(color.teal, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
    slLbl    := label.new(bar_index, slLevel, text = "SL " + str.tostring(slLevel, "#.##"), style = label.style_label_left,  color = color.new(color.red, 20),  textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
    entryPriceLbl := label.new(bar_index, na, text = "LONG NQ ENTRY\n" + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + "\n" + str.tostring(tradeContracts) + " contract(s)", style = label.style_triangleup, yloc = yloc.belowbar, color = color.new(color.green, 0), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, force_overlay = true)

if stopSig
    strategy.close_all(comment = "Stop")
    posState := 0

if exitSig
    strategy.close_all(comment = "Exit")
    posState := 0

if segmentExitSig
    strategy.close_all(comment = "Segment End")
    posState := 0

if stopSig or exitSig or segmentExitSig
    // Informational NQ-leg $ P&L (see companion indicator's identical sign
    // convention comment): closingPosState == 1 -> NQ leg is short, profits
    // when price falls; == -1 -> NQ leg is long, profits when price rises.
    // Uses the snapshot taken above, since posState is already reset to 0
    // by the individual stop/exit/segment-end blocks above this one.
    exitPriceNQ = close
    pnlPts = closingPosState == 1 ? (entryPriceNQ - exitPriceNQ) : (exitPriceNQ - entryPriceNQ)
    cumPnlUSD += pnlPts * pointValue * tradeContracts
    killSwitch := killSwitch or (cumPnlUSD <= -maxLossUSD)
    entryLevel     := na
    tpLevel        := na
    slLevel        := na
    entryPriceNQ   := na
    slPriceAtEntry := na
    tradeContracts := 0
    label.delete(entryLbl)
    label.delete(tpLbl)
    label.delete(slLbl)
    label.delete(entryPriceLbl)
    entryLbl := na
    tpLbl    := na
    slLbl    := na
    entryPriceLbl := na

// Live-updating TP/SL implied NQ price for the open trade -- recomputed
// every bar, not stored in `var` (see NQ PRICE PROJECTION above).
tpPriceNQ = posState == 1 ? f_impliedNQPrice(-exitZ) : posState == -1 ? f_impliedNQPrice(exitZ) : na
slPriceNQ = posState == 1 ? f_impliedNQPrice(-stopZ) : posState == -1 ? f_impliedNQPrice(stopZ) : na

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TRADING HALTED WARNING -- informational mirror of strategy.risk.max_drawdown()
// tripping (see companion indicator's identical block).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
var label haltLbl = na
if killSwitch and barstate.islast
    label.delete(haltLbl)
    haltLbl := label.new(bar_index, na, text = "🛑 MAX LOSS HIT -- TRADING HALTED\nCumulative NQ P&L: $" + str.tostring(cumPnlUSD, "#.##"), style = label.style_label_down, yloc = yloc.abovebar, color = color.new(color.red, 0), textcolor = color.white, size = size.large, force_overlay = true)
bgcolor(killSwitch ? color.new(color.red, 85) : na, title = "Trading Halted Shading", force_overlay = true)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PLOTS -- same visual layout as the companion indicator, for side-by-side
// comparison of signal timing against the Strategy Tester's trade markers.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(zscore, title = "Z-Score", color = color.new(color.blue, 0), linewidth = 2)

hline(0,        "Zero",    color = color.gray,                 linestyle = hline.style_solid)
hline(entryZ,   "Entry +", color = color.new(color.orange, 0), linestyle = hline.style_dashed)
hline(-entryZ,  "Entry -", color = color.new(color.orange, 0), linestyle = hline.style_dashed)
hline(exitZ,    "Exit +",  color = color.new(color.teal, 0),   linestyle = hline.style_dotted)
hline(-exitZ,   "Exit -",  color = color.new(color.teal, 0),   linestyle = hline.style_dotted)
hline(stopZ,    "Stop +",  color = color.new(color.red, 0),    linestyle = hline.style_solid)
hline(-stopZ,   "Stop -",  color = color.new(color.red, 0),    linestyle = hline.style_solid)

// Open-trade entry / take-profit / stop-loss levels (z-score units -- see
// the state-machine comment above). style_linebr breaks the line once the
// value goes na, so each trade gets its own bounded pair of levels.
plot(posState != 0 ? entryLevel : na, title = "Entry Level (z)",       color = color.new(color.gray, 40), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plot(posState != 0 ? tpLevel    : na, title = "Take Profit Level (z)", color = color.new(color.teal, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2)
plot(posState != 0 ? slLevel    : na, title = "Stop Loss Level (z)",   color = color.new(color.red, 0),   style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2)

// Same levels, on the NQ price axis, pushed onto the main chart via
// force_overlay so they appear directly on the NQ candles. entryPriceNQ is
// the actual fill price (fixed); tpPriceNQ/slPriceNQ are the live implied-
// price estimate and will visibly shift bar to bar (see NQ PRICE PROJECTION).
plot(posState != 0 ? entryPriceNQ : na, title = "Entry Price (NQ)",            color = color.new(color.gray, 40), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1, force_overlay = true)
plot(posState != 0 ? tpPriceNQ    : na, title = "Take Profit (NQ, live est.)", color = color.new(color.teal, 0),  style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2, force_overlay = true)
plot(posState != 0 ? slPriceNQ    : na, title = "Stop Loss (NQ, live est.)",   color = color.new(color.red, 0),   style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 2, force_overlay = true)

// Always-on price reference bands -- the lines above only draw while a
// trade is actually open, so on a quiet chart with no active signal nothing
// shows up on the NQ candles. These are the same +-entryZ/+-exitZ/+-stopZ
// thresholds projected onto the NQ price axis via f_impliedNQPrice(),
// plotted continuously regardless of position state (see the companion
// indicator's identical block for the full rationale).
entryHiPriceNQ = f_impliedNQPrice(entryZ)
entryLoPriceNQ = f_impliedNQPrice(-entryZ)
exitHiPriceNQ  = f_impliedNQPrice(exitZ)
exitLoPriceNQ  = f_impliedNQPrice(-exitZ)
stopHiPriceNQ  = f_impliedNQPrice(stopZ)
stopLoPriceNQ  = f_impliedNQPrice(-stopZ)

plot(showLevels ? entryHiPriceNQ : na, title = "Entry Threshold + (NQ)", color = color.new(color.orange, 40), style = plot.style_line, linewidth = 1, force_overlay = true)
plot(showLevels ? entryLoPriceNQ : na, title = "Entry Threshold - (NQ)", color = color.new(color.orange, 40), style = plot.style_line, linewidth = 1, force_overlay = true)
plot(showLevels ? exitHiPriceNQ  : na, title = "Exit Threshold + (NQ)",  color = color.new(color.teal, 55),   style = plot.style_line, linewidth = 1, force_overlay = true)
plot(showLevels ? exitLoPriceNQ  : na, title = "Exit Threshold - (NQ)",  color = color.new(color.teal, 55),   style = plot.style_line, linewidth = 1, force_overlay = true)
plot(showLevels ? stopHiPriceNQ  : na, title = "Stop Threshold + (NQ)",  color = color.new(color.red, 55),    style = plot.style_line, linewidth = 1, force_overlay = true)
plot(showLevels ? stopLoPriceNQ  : na, title = "Stop Threshold - (NQ)",  color = color.new(color.red, 55),    style = plot.style_line, linewidth = 1, force_overlay = true)

bgCol = posState == 1 ? color.new(color.green, 90) : posState == -1 ? color.new(color.red, 90) : na
bgcolor(showBg ? bgCol : na, title = "Position State Shading (pane)")
bgcolor(showBg ? bgCol : na, title = "Position State Shading (chart)", force_overlay = true)

// Segment window shading on the main chart, so it's obvious which bars the
// active segment covers regardless of "All History" being selected.
bgcolor(showBg and not inSegment ? color.new(color.gray, 95) : na, title = "Outside Active Segment", force_overlay = true)

plotshape(showMarkers and longEntrySig  ? zscore : na, title = "Long Spread Entry (Short NQ)",  style = shape.triangleup,   location = location.absolute, color = color.new(color.green, 0),  size = size.small)
plotshape(showMarkers and shortEntrySig ? zscore : na, title = "Short Spread Entry (Long NQ)",  style = shape.triangledown, location = location.absolute, color = color.new(color.red, 0),    size = size.small)
plotshape(showMarkers and exitSig       ? zscore : na, title = "Exit to Flat",                  style = shape.xcross,       location = location.absolute, color = color.new(color.gray, 0),   size = size.small)
plotshape(showMarkers and stopSig       ? zscore : na, title = "Stop-Out",                      style = shape.diamond,      location = location.absolute, color = color.new(color.red, 0),    size = size.normal)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STATS TABLE -- for the authoritative trade count / win rate / net P&L per
// segment, use the Strategy Tester's own "List of Trades" and "Performance
// Summary" tabs (switch segmentChoice above and re-run to compare them).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table infoTable = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 13, border_width = 1, force_overlay = true)

if showTable and barstate.islast
    posText = posState == 1 ? "LONG SPREAD (short NQ)" : posState == -1 ? "SHORT SPREAD (long NQ)" : "FLAT"
    budgetLeftUSD = math.max(0.0, maxLossUSD + cumPnlUSD)
    riskTableColor = killSwitch ? color.new(color.red, 60) : color.new(color.gray, 80)

    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 0, "Segment",  bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 0, segmentChoice, bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 1, "Z-Score",  bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 1, str.tostring(zscore, "#.##"), bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 2, "Beta",     bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 2, str.tostring(beta, "#.####"), bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 3, "Position", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 3, killSwitch ? "HALTED" : posText, bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = killSwitch ? color.red : posState == 1 ? color.lime : posState == -1 ? color.red : color.white)
    // Always-on prospective entry thresholds, so the table is informative
    // even while flat (see ALWAYS-ON PRICE REFERENCE BANDS above).
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 4, "Entry Threshold +", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 4, na(entryHiPriceNQ) ? "N/A" : str.tostring(entryHiPriceNQ, format.mintick), bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.orange)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 5, "Entry Threshold -", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 5, na(entryLoPriceNQ) ? "N/A" : str.tostring(entryLoPriceNQ, format.mintick), bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.orange)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 6, "Entry Price (NQ)", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 6, posState != 0 ? str.tostring(entryPriceNQ, format.mintick) : "-- (no open trade)", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 7, "Take Profit (NQ)", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 7, posState == 0 ? "-- (no open trade)" : na(tpPriceNQ) ? "N/A" : str.tostring(tpPriceNQ, format.mintick) + " (est.)", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.teal)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 8, "Stop Loss (NQ)", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 8, posState == 0 ? "-- (no open trade)" : na(slPriceNQ) ? "N/A" : str.tostring(slPriceNQ, format.mintick) + " (est.)", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.red)
    // Position sizing / risk governor (see Prop Firm Risk Management inputs).
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 9, "Contracts (qty)", bgcolor = riskTableColor, text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 9, posState != 0 ? str.tostring(tradeContracts) : "--", bgcolor = riskTableColor, text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 10, "Cumulative P&L ($)", bgcolor = riskTableColor, text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 10, "$" + str.tostring(cumPnlUSD, "#.##"), bgcolor = riskTableColor, text_color = cumPnlUSD >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 11, "Loss Budget Left", bgcolor = riskTableColor, text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 11, killSwitch ? "$0 -- HALTED" : "$" + str.tostring(budgetLeftUSD, "#.##"), bgcolor = riskTableColor, text_color = killSwitch ? color.red : color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 12, "Point Value", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 12, "$" + str.tostring(pointValue, "#.##") + "/pt (" + syminfo.ticker + ")", bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 80), text_color = color.white)

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ALERTS -- same four events as the companion indicator.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(longEntrySig,  title = "Long Spread Entry",  message = "NQ/Basket pairs: LONG SPREAD entry (short NQ leg) on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(shortEntrySig, title = "Short Spread Entry", message = "NQ/Basket pairs: SHORT SPREAD entry (long NQ leg) on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(exitSig,       title = "Exit to Flat",       message = "NQ/Basket pairs: exit to FLAT on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(stopSig,       title = "Stop-Out",           message = "NQ/Basket pairs: STOPPED OUT on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
